"505","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 505 Arabic Hadees: 1920"
"506","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the believers have been saved from the Fire and are secure, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of you will dispute with his companion regarding a right he has in this world more intensely than the believers will dispute with their Lord on behalf of their brothers who were admitted into the Fire.They will say: 'Our Lord, our brothers used to pray with us, fast with us, and perform Hajj with us (and fight alongside us), yet You admitted them into the Fire.'He will say: 'Go and bring out those whom you recognize among them.' So they will come to them and recognize them by their faces, for the Fire will not consume their faces. Some of them the Fire will have seized up to half their shins, and some up to their ankles. They will bring them out and say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those You commanded us to.'Then He will say: 'Bring out those who had in their hearts the weight of a dinar of faith,' then 'those who had the weight of half a dinar,' until He says: 'Those who had the weight of an atom (dharr).'Abu Sa'id said: 'Whoever does not believe this, let him read this verse: ""Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] an atom's weight; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward."" (An-Nisa: 40)Then they will say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those You commanded us; no one with any good in him remains in the Fire.'Then Allah will say: 'The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded, and there remains the Most Merciful of the merciful.'He will then take a handful from the Fire—or He said: two handfuls—of people who never did any good for Allah at all, who have been burnt until they became charcoal (humam). They will be brought to a water called the Water of Life, and it will be poured over them, and they will sprout as the seed sprouts in the silt left by a flood. They will emerge from their bodies like pearls, with seals on their necks [reading]: 'The Freed Ones of Allah.'It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise. Whatever you wish for or see, it is yours, and with Me is even better than that.'They will say: 'Our Lord, what is better than that?'He will say: 'My Pleasure upon you, so I shall never be angry with you ever again.'"""
