"518","On the authority of Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! I ask you about something you know and I am ignorant of: Is there an hour of the night or day in which prayer is disliked?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you pray the dawn prayer (Fajr), then refrain from prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. Then when it has risen, pray, for the prayer is witnessed and accepted until the sun is at its zenith like a spear. Then when it is at its zenith, that hour is when Hell is heated up and its gates are opened until it passes from your right eyebrow. Then when it has passed from your right eyebrow, pray, for the prayer is witnessed and accepted until you pray the afternoon prayer (Asr). Then leave prayer until the sun sets."""
