"618","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, marfūʿan: ""Six characteristics: no Muslim dies while engaged in one of them except that it is guaranteed upon Allah to admit him into Paradise: a man who goes out fighting in Allah's cause—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who follows a funeral procession—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who visits a sick person—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who performs ablution and perfects it, then goes out to the mosque for his prayer—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who comes to an imām, not coming to him except to excuse him and honor him—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; and a man in his house who does not backbite a Muslim, nor bring upon them wrath or punishment—if he dies, it is guaranteed upon Allah."""
