"648","On the authority of Abu Musa, who said: ""I and my companions who had arrived with me on the ship were staying at Baqi' Buthan, while the Prophet ﷺ was in Medina. A group from among them would take turns waiting for the Prophet ﷺ at the time of the Isha prayer every night. It so happened that my companions and I coincided with the Prophet ﷺ, but he had some occupation regarding some of his affairs, so he delayed the prayer until the middle of the night. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out and led them in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said to those present: 'Take it easy! Rejoice, for it is from Allah's favor upon you that no one among the people is praying at this hour except you,' or he said: 'No one has prayed this prayer except you.' He (the narrator) said: 'He does not know which of the two statements he said.' Abu Musa said: 'So we returned rejoicing at what we had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'His saying: (Ibharra) means: it became the middle. And the 'Buhra' of everything is its middle. It was said: (Ibhar al-layl) is when its stars appear and it becomes illuminated; the first (meaning) is more common."""
